      "license": "Public domain",
      "artist": "NPS staff",
      "description": "Interpretive staff working in cabin's kitchen\nLincoln Boyhood National Memorial preserves the site of the farm where Abraham Lincoln spent 14 formative years of his life, from the ages of 7 to 21. He and his family moved to Indiana in 1816 and stayed until 1830 when they moved on to Illinois. The time he spent here helped shape the man that went on to lead the country. This site is our most direct tie with that time of his life.\nKeywords: libo; living history; National memorials; Interpretive programs; Presidents; Homes; Lincoln; Abraham; 1809-1865",
